Package: gog
Title: Grammar of Graphics
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("psychometrician", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "psychometrician@gmail.com")
Description: Draw a plot by describing it. You name a table, a mark to
    draw, and which column goes to which part of the picture, and one
    engine turns that description into an SVG. The same description is
    written the same way in R, 'Python', 'Julia' and 'JavaScript', and is
    drawn by a single engine written in 'Rust' that ships inside the
    package, so nothing has to be installed or added to the path.
License: Apache License (== 2.0)
URL: https://github.com/psychometrician/gog,
    https://psychometrician.github.io/gog-book/
BugReports: https://github.com/psychometrician/gog/issues
SystemRequirements: Cargo (Rust's package manager), rustc
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends:
    R (>= 4.3)
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Imports:
    jsonlite,
    utils
Suggests:
    DBI,
    RSQLite,
    gapminder,
    IRdisplay,
    knitr,
    pkgload,
    repr,
    testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.0.0
